# Native integration corpus, both hosts (scripts/verify-integration.sh).
#
# name|hosts|opt|source|exit|stdout|args|deps|extra[|suite-members]
#
# hosts: all, linux or windows. Linux-only rows are the System V C ABI
#   fixtures, raw Linux syscalls (syscall_arg_alias, dead_frame_store), the
#   poison-on-reclaim trap Windows cannot fire (arena_poison_stale_array_trap)
#   and lsp_position_edit_smoke; Windows-only rows are the Win64 C ABI
#   fixtures, the VirtualAlloc abort transcript and the rooted NtCreateFile
#   boundary.
# opt: the levels the row runs at, in order. `-` is the default level the
#   batched pre-pass compiles; 0, 1 and 2 compile the row standalone at that
#   level, so a claim that only holds at one level can sit beside the default
#   row. A row with several levels runs as `name` (for -) and `name_optN`; a
#   row with one level keeps its name. scripts/expand-integration-manifest.awk
#   expands one host's rows.
# stdout: "-" for empty, @path for an exact repository file, or printf escapes.
# args, deps: space-separated, "-" for none.
# extra: "-", stage-stdlib, expected-stderr:<printf escapes> or
#   stage-stdlib+expected-stderr:<printf escapes>; $SRC in an expected stderr is
#   the staged source the compiler reports (target/integration-verify/HOST/ROW/ROW.tl).
# suite-members: space-separated smoke drivers the row's source runs.
